This death was frustrating in that way that all deaths caused by
obvious mistakes are.

My Gnome wizard was having a hell of a game.  I knew I was going to
ascend almost from the first moment since I didn't get any wishes in
minetown.  My games typically end early when I get lucky with
equipment, so in this case, I wasn't getting any gear.

I managed to find a well placed altar around level 7 which I set up as
a pudding farm.  The only pudding I had was a brown, which I hate since
they only leave corpses about 1/4 of the time.  Black puddings are much
better for this activity.   I grew bored of this pretty quickly and
abandoned it after a few thousand turns.

Did Sokoban, got amulet, found a BoH somewhere, did Ludios, and onward
down to Medusa and The Castle.  I completed the quest sometime in here
as well, and didn't have any difficulty with it.  I used one wish from
a Lamp to get SDSM.

After all this, I decide to start sacrificing to complete my spellbook
collection.  I had acquired a Create Monster spellbook, so that plus
the Eye of the Aethiopica plus a ring of slow digestion had me
sacrificing indefinitely.  I briefly considered an extinctionist
challenge, but decided it was too boring.

After about 20000 turns of this, I'm at a natural HP of over 350, my
naked AC was 5 due to an unfortunate Gnome sacrifice or two.  I decide
it's time to ascend.  So I enchant everything up, I had gotten about
five magic markers during my sac fest.  I also had received both Fire
and Frost Brand, speed boots, dex gloves.  The only item I was missing
was a helm of brilliance which I decided to use a wish on.  I mixed up
about 50 full healing potions which brought my HP to 750.  Then I
genocided L, h, ;, and T.  I re-read some spellbooks and dumped
everything else in my stash.  Then I started descending.

In Medusa's lair, in her very room, I encounter a yellow "c".  Now,
I've killed probably 50 of these so far, so I didn't blink.  I knew my
gloves were on.  I had a lizard corpse ready.  I was not wearing my
AoLS since I was nigh invincible.  I killed the stupid little "c" and
moved on.  I had a bunch of pets, so I was hitting "esc" after every
move to skip all their stupid messages.

DYWYPI?

I had escaped past the part about stiffening up.  I had stone to flesh
memorized.  I had a lizard corpse.  I was not in Gehennom and could
have prayed.  I could have been wearing my AoLS.  I could have gone a
little slower and read the *@#& messages.

And to top that off, no bones generated.  Although, at 2.5 million
points, this was my highest scoring non-ascension ever.



